{"availability":"available","full":"jinzhezenggroup/xtbloom","name":"xtbloom","description":"Native, batched GFN2-xTB inference for C, C++, Python, and CUDA.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Cuda","stars":3,"forks":2,"created":"2026-08-02T05:52:18Z","updated":"2026-10-15T15:18:52Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://xtbloom.jinzhezeng.group/","topics":["cuda","wasm","xtb"],"demo":"https://xtbloom.jinzhezeng.group/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T07:10:37.941Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T07:10:37.941Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T07:10:37.941Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T07:26:45.518Z","stars":3,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-17T07:10:37.941Z","stars":3,"forks":2}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Native, batched GFN-xTB inference for C, C++, Python, and CUDA.","Try it in your browser · Python guide · C/C++ guide · Documentation","xTBloom is a C++17 library for applications that need energies, analytic forces, and atomic charges for many small and medium molecular systems. Its CPU and CUDA backends share one stable C ABI, with Python, ASE, and dpdata interfaces built on the same native execution path."],"features":["Native ragged batches. Differently sized molecules share one call without","One model-aware API. Restricted and unrestricted GFN1-xTB and GFN2-xTB","Failure isolation. SCC or eigensolver failure is local to one batch","Analytic derivatives and embedding. Both models return CPU/CUDA energies,","Reusable execution state. Contexts retain CPU workers, CUDA workspaces,"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jinzhezenggroup/xtbloom/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"362106b25a0fac3660d05bcd3bea6b537bd2e7bd3456dd03e54488a4089409c6","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:45.607Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:45.607Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Native, batched GFN-xTB inference for C, C++, Python, and CUDA.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/